From b322e81778b99fb59c772e73869c75510dfa8335 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 375/488] soh: name the 33 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_bigokuta.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 33 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c; updating their references touches 3 files in total.

  * func_809BCE3C -> EnBigokuta_UpdateOrbitPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: places the octopus 263 units out from its home
    position along the yaw its facing implies

  * func_809BCEBC -> EnBigokuta_SpawnWaterRipple
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rings the water surface every seventh frame
    while the body sits near it

  * func_809BCF68 -> EnBigokuta_SpawnWakeSplash
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spawns the ripple and splash trailing behind
    the moving octopus, with its splash sound

  * func_809BD1C8 -> EnBigokuta_SpawnLandingSplash
    deduced, confidence HIGH: four corner splashes with the landing sounds
    and a quake

  * func_809BD2E4 -> EnBigokuta_TurnParent
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps the parent actor's yaw toward this
    actor's target

  * func_809BD318 -> EnBigokuta_SetupIntroWait
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops the idle animation underwater and arms
    the 121-frame intro wait

  * func_809BD370 -> EnBigokuta_SetupJumpIn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the 21-frame leap and plays the jump
    sound

  * func_809BD3AC -> EnBigokuta_SetupTurnToStart
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drops the octopus onto its starting point on
    the ring and arms the turn

  * func_809BD3E0 -> EnBigokuta_SetupWaitBeforeCircle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the 40-frame pause before the circling
    begins

  * func_809BD3F8 -> EnBigokuta_SetupCircle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: morphs to the swimming loop, arms the
    350-frame circling window and turns the colliders on

  * func_809BD47C -> EnBigokuta_SetupBounce
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the damageEffect 0xF response: turns AC off
    and arms a 16-frame arc; whether this reads as a bounce or a recoil is
    not settled by the code

  * func_809BD4A4 -> EnBigokuta_SetupTurnAround
    deduced, confidence HIGH: records the opposite heading in world.rot.x
    and morphs to the idle loop while it turns

  * func_809BD524 -> EnBigokuta_SetupStunned
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays NA_SE_EN_DAIOCTA_MAHI with the blue
    color filter, shortening the stun when the hit came from a projectile

  * func_809BD5E0 -> EnBigokuta_SetupDamage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the flinch animation with the red color
    filter for 24 frames

  * func_809BD658 -> EnBigokuta_SetupDeath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the death animation with
    NA_SE_EN_DAIOCTA_DEAD2

  * func_809BD6B8 -> EnBigokuta_SetupSpin
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the spin duration from whether the
    octopus is facing the player and turns AC off

  * func_809BD768 -> EnBigokuta_SetupSink
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks a new circling direction, drops
    targeting and plays NA_SE_EN_DAIOCTA_SINK

  * func_809BD7F0 -> EnBigokuta_SetupResurface
    deduced, confidence HIGH: re-aims the ring position at the player's side
    of the arena before rising

  * func_809BD84C -> EnBigokuta_IntroWait
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the intro wait down, calling out twice
    and starting the miniboss music

  * func_809BD8DC -> EnBigokuta_JumpIn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arcs the octopus out of the water onto the
    ring, splashing and rumbling on landing

  * func_809BDAE8 -> EnBigokuta_TurnToStart
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns onto the home yaw, then becomes an enemy
    and moves on

  * func_809BDB90 -> EnBigokuta_WaitBeforeCircle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the pause out and starts the miniboss
    music for the params 3 spawn

  * func_809BDC08 -> EnBigokuta_Circle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: circles the ring, speeding up or slowing down
    with the player's distance and facing, and picks the next state when its
    windows expire

  * func_809BDF34 -> EnBigokuta_Bounce
    deduced, confidence GUESS: arcs the body 100 units up and back down on a
    sine, splashing on landing before resuming the circle

  * func_809BDFC8 -> EnBigokuta_TurnAround
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns onto the recorded opposite heading,
    flips the circling direction and resumes

  * func_809BE058 -> EnBigokuta_Stunned
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds still for the stun, shoving the player
    off whichever collider they touch

  * func_809BE180 -> EnBigokuta_Damage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rides the knockback arc, then either resumes
    or dies according to remaining health

  * func_809BE26C -> EnBigokuta_Death
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spins, puffs dust, shrinks away, clears the
    room and drops a collectible

  * func_809BE3E4 -> EnBigokuta_Spin
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spins in place, then picks the direction it
    was turned toward and resumes circling

  * func_809BE4A4 -> EnBigokuta_Sink
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drops 10 units a frame while spinning until
    200 below home, then resurfaces elsewhere

  * func_809BE518 -> EnBigokuta_Resurface
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rises back to home height, restores targeting
    and resumes circling

  * func_809BE568 -> EnBigokuta_UpdateColliders
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rotates the jntsph and both cylinders into
